      "default": "A calm, plain-English look at what colic actually is, the real reasons feeds go sideways, and the small changes that tend to make the biggest difference — including the one most parents overlook."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_caption",
      "label": "Hero illustration caption",
      "default": "Colic is common, exhausting — and more manageable than it feels at 3am"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Author byline"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "author_name",
      "label": "Author name (falls back to article author)",
      "default": "Dr. Emily Hartman, RD"
